# Filesystem Rules

Use pathlib.Path for filesystem paths.

Do not hardcode absolute Windows paths.

Do not assume a specific user's home directory.

Keep development paths portable.

Do not write application data into arbitrary filesystem locations.

Do not implement PyInstaller-specific path handling during the Django prototype phase.

When filesystem paths are required, prefer paths derived from Django's BASE_DIR or an explicitly configured application-data directory.

Do not introduce complex packaging-specific path logic unless the current development phase requires it.